<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Beta terms — LowEndInsight</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/lei.css">
</head>
<body>
<main class="prose">
  <h1>Beta terms</h1>

  <h2>This is a beta</h2>
  <p>
    LowEndInsight is being tested in the open. It may be unavailable, it may
    return wrong answers, and features may change or disappear. Do not use it as
    the only input to a decision that matters.
  </p>

  <h2>Analysis is free during beta</h2>
  <p>
    <%= if guide.beta? do %>
      Nothing is charged today. Accounts are limited to
      <%= LeiService.AgentGuide.number(guide.free_monthly_analyses) %> analyses a
      month, which is what keeps the beta affordable for us.
    <% else %>
      Beta has ended and analysis is charged at the published rates.
    <% end %>
    Prices are published at <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> so that when beta
    ends nothing about the change is a surprise. We will tell account holders
    before charging begins.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty, and use is at your own risk</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>The service is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as
    available&rdquo;, with no warranty of any kind, express or implied.</strong>
    That includes, without limitation, any implied warranty of merchantability,
    fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or non-infringement.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Any use of this service, and any reliance on its output, is entirely
    at your own risk.</strong> The reports are automated measurements of public
    repository metadata. They may be incomplete, out of date, or wrong. They are
    not a security audit, not a licence review, not legal or professional advice,
    and not a statement that any dependency is safe to use.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for deciding what to do with the output and for
    verifying anything you act on. To the fullest extent permitted by law we
    accept no liability for any loss or damage &mdash; direct, indirect,
    incidental, consequential or otherwise &mdash; arising from use of the
    service, from inability to use it, or from decisions made on the basis of
    what it reports.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Public repository data.</strong> We clone repositories you ask
      about, compute metrics, and keep the resulting report in a shared cache for
      30 days. Reports are shared: if you and someone else ask about the same
      commit, you get the same cached answer.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your account.</strong> An organisation record, hashed API keys, and
      a count of analyses used per billing period.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We do not store repository contents.</strong> A clone is deleted
      once its metrics are computed. What persists is the report: counts, dates,
      contributor names as they appear in public commit metadata, and risk
      ratings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Private repositories are not supported.</strong> Do not point this
      at one. There is no path for supplying credentials, and a private
      repository will simply fail to clone.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ending it</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using the service at any time and ask us to delete your
    account. We may end the beta, or an individual account, at any time. If we
    end the beta we will keep the cached public reports, which contain nothing
    of yours.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms will change as the service leaves beta. The version in force is
    whatever this page says; it is generated from the running deployment rather
    than pasted, so it cannot describe a mode the service is not in.
  </p>

  <p class="footnote">
    Questions: <a href="https://github.com/kitplummer/lowendinsight/issues">open an issue</a>.
  </p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
